		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4926&amp;p=36030#p36030"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Blank screen on a previously working radio is usually caused by a poor connection on the ribbon cable between the main board and the front panel. You would need to open the radio and reseat both ends of the cable. <br><br>Colin G4EML</div></blockquote>Thks, not easy to open it but that did the trick  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy">.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8186">PH7R</a> — Sat Mar 01, 2025 8:08 pm</p><hr />
